      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`top_k_top_p_min_p_sampling_from_probs_torch` asserts `sampling_seed is None` whenever min-p is on, with a TODO saying the filtered probabilities would have to be renormalized before `multinomial_with_seed`. So any request that sets both `sampling_seed` and `min_p` fails on the torch sampling backend.\n\nRenormalizing is not needed. `multinomial_with_seed` is a Gumbel-max: it takes `argmax(log w + gumbel_noise)` per row. Dividing a row by its sum only subtracts the same constant from every `log w` in that row, so the argmax, and the sampled token, are unchanged. Tokens zeroed by min-p become `log 0 = -inf` and are never picked.\n\nThe same function already relies on this: top-k and top-p zero entries of `probs_sort` without renormalizing, and the seeded branch passes those unnormalized weights to `multinomial_with_seed`. The Ascend path (`top_k_top_p_min_p_sampling_from_logits_ascend`) and the MLX sampler (`hardware_backend/mlx/sampling.py`, \"Gumbel-max over the UNNORMALIZED masked weights ... also what keeps a seeded row well-defined under min_p\") already sample seeded min-p rows this way.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/layers/sampler.py`: remove the `sampling_seed is None` assert and the renormalization TODO from the min-p branch of `top_k_top_p_min_p_sampling_from_probs_torch`. The min-p filter itself is unchanged.\n- `test/registered/sampling/test_seeded_min_p_sampling.py` (new, 1-GPU CUDA CI next to `test_deterministic_gumbel_u1.py`):\n  - Seeded min-p sampling over 4096 rows returns exactly the tokens of a seeded draw from the explicitly renormalized min-p weights.\n  - 200k seeded draws from one row never pick a min-p filtered token, and the frequencies match the renormalized min-p distribution within 0.01.\n\nBoth tests fail on `main` with the removed assert and pass with this change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOnly requests that set both `sampling_seed` and `min_p` take the changed path; they previously raised. Other requests are unaffected.\n\nH200, 200k seeded draws from probabilities `[0.40, 0.30, 0.15, 0.10, 0.05]` with `min_p=0.3`:\n\n| Weights passed to `multinomial_with_seed` | token 0 | token 1 | token 2 | tokens 3, 4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| min-p filtered, not renormalized | 0.4691 | 0.3535 | 0.1774 | 0 |\n| min-p filtered, renormalized | 0.4691 | 0.3535 | 0.1774 | 0 |\n| target (renormalized min-p distribution) | 0.4706 | 0.3529 | 0.1765 | 0 |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo change: the removed lines are an assert.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41375601566](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41375601566)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41375601441](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41375601441)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41375601474](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41375601474)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
